<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Worker">

  <!--
    TcpAdapter (C043) — hardware GPS tracker ingest: GT06 / JT/T 808 / H02 / generic-NMEA.

    Terminate the device socket on 5023-5026, authenticate its IMEI against provisioning-svc
    (T-01/T-03/T-12), decode the binary or ASCII frame into the canonical PositionSample, and
    publish it into EMQX on `veh/{vehicleId}/pos/live` (or `/pos/replay`) as the `svc-` bridge user.
    Downlink commands travel the other way: `veh/{vehicleId}/cmd` -> a protocol-native command frame
    on the open socket (§7.7.5). A half-closed socket publishes the retained `status=offline` that
    emulates an MQTT last will (T-04).

    Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Worker, NOT Sdk.Web: `mqtt-topics.md` §7 says "tcp-adapter is one StatefulSet
    per protocol family and has no HTTP surface", and D7' §5.1 gives it a TCP-socket liveness probe
    (`nc -z 127.0.0.1 5023`) instead of /health/live for exactly that reason. So there is no Kestrel
    here and no `AddMageRideDefaults` — the kernel's HTTP half has nothing to configure. The pieces
    that are not HTTP (Postgres, Redis, telemetry, the MQTT session-token issuer) are registered
    directly in TcpAdapterApplication.

    The image is nevertheless `aspnet:*-alpine` rather than D7' §2.2's `runtime:*-alpine`:
    MageRide.Shared carries `FrameworkReference Microsoft.AspNetCore.App`, and backend/CLAUDE.md
    requires every service to reference it. See the Dockerfile.

    NOT here: the protocol *decision* of which vehicle a device belongs to (provisioning-svc, C030),
    the seq dedupe and anti-spoof filter (position-processor-svc, C039), the Timescale write (C040),
    and the LWT *consumers* (trip-state, dispatch, fleet-health).

    Verify: dotnet test backend/src/TcpAdapter.Tests -c Release
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>MageRide.TcpAdapter</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>MageRide.TcpAdapter</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <UserSecretsId>mageride-tcp-adapter</UserSecretsId>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\MageRide.Shared\MageRide.Shared.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The adapter is an MQTT *client* of EMQX, publishing on behalf of devices that cannot speak
         MQTT themselves, and a subscriber of `veh/+/cmd` for the downlink. Same client the bridge
         uses (C038) so both halves of the plane agree about protocol version and QoS. -->
    <PackageReference Include="MQTTnet" />
    <!-- `imei:{imei}` (T-03), the `prov:tracker` revocation channel (T-12) and the
         `veh:driver:{vehicleId}` standby binding the T-11 gate reads. -->
    <PackageReference Include="StackExchange.Redis" />
    <!-- registry.vehicles.mode / vehicle_type — read-only, one indexed lookup per device connect.
         See Modes/VehicleProfiles.cs for why the adapter needs a database at all. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Dapper" />
    <PackageReference Include="Npgsql" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="TcpAdapter.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
